messages:
maria_cs: FYI — Acme onboarding is hitting repeated 429s on our preflight calls since ~10:23 UTC. Spike concentrated in eu-west. They reported flakey init in the browser and a lot of parallel tabs.
maria_cs: Logs show HTTP 429 with headers: `X-RateLimit-Limit: 1200`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0`, `Retry-After: 60`. No other 5xx.
sam_sdk: Thanks — are they doing the default browser SDK flow (one preflight per page/tab)? That fanout often causes ephemeral token storms. Can you paste their init snippet?
maria_cs: Pasting sanitized snippet they used: ```js
Redwood.init({ key: "ephemeral:...", preflight: true, parallelPreflight: true });
```
rahul_eng: I pulled edge metrics — pattern is many short-lived ephemeral tokens created within a 5s window, which triggers our per-tenant sliding-window limiter. Behavior matches client-side fanout + no jitter.
rahul_eng: Short-term mitigations: client jitter + reuse ephemeral token for N seconds. Longer-term: we can temporary bump their burst quota for onboarding.
luis_sre: I created ticket #4478 to request a limited quota bump and inserted a 1s per-token splay at the edge for that tenant.
luis_sre: deploy-bot, can you push the splay rule?
deploy-bot: rolling out tenant splay rule for tenant=acme-prod, change id=chg-4478. Start -> OK. Edge config propagated to eu-west in ~20s.
sam_sdk: Quick client-side fixes to share with the customer: 1) reuse ephemeral token for 30s instead of minting per attempt; 2) add randomized delay between preflights (250-1000ms); 3) cap concurrent preflights to 3. Example snippet: ```js
// basic splay + reuse
const token = await getEphemeralToken();
await Promise.all(tabs.slice(0,3).map(async (t, i) => {
  await delay(250 + Math.random()*750);
  await Redwood.init({ key: token, preflight: true });
}));
```
maria_cs: Passing these to the customer now. I'll ask them to deploy the patch and confirm after two deployments.
rahul_eng: If they still see 429s after client changes, we'll enable fallback to cached prefix on the runtime to reduce preflight pressure and re-evaluate rate window sizing.
maria_cs: Great — I'll keep this thread updated. Thanks all :thumbsup:
